  "news": [
    {
      "title": "New Hire: Jiatao Gu, Member of Technical Staff, New York City",
      "url": "https://ami.frenchtechjournal.com/team/jiatao-gu",
      "source": "The AMI Observatory",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-03"
    }
  ],
  "xPosts": [
    {
      "text": "We need not only videobench, but InteractionBench! Multimodal systems need to know when and how to respond, and when to stay silent, in real time. In my view, this is a stepping stone toward physical AI in the real world. \n\nLed by my first-year PhD student @EnxinSong at Penn! https://t.co/yvZNCqLcg8",
      "url": "https://x.com/thoma_gu/status/2107511515284988376",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-06T16:41:15.000Z"
    },
    {
      "text": "Happy to share both STARFlow2 and NTM were accepted to #NeurIPS2026, onwards our exploration of scalable normalizing flows! 🎉\nhttps://t.co/kKLIlNxO4v\nhttps://t.co/NDID5iGxSp\n\nI'll also be at #COLM2026 in SF Oct 6–9 — happy to chat LLMs, world models, and everything in between!!",
      "url": "https://x.com/thoma_gu/status/2107248612048601236",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-05T23:16:34.000Z"
    },
    {
      "text": "Video benchmarks aren't saturated, they're just easy to game. We introduce Video-Index by dropping all shortcut-solvable questions across 115 benchmarks — key findings: Astra 79.3% beats humans 55%, while open models &lt;20%. Led by my incredible first-year PhD student @EnxinSong ! https://t.co/dxlP1FXzWO",
      "url": "https://x.com/thoma_gu/status/2105855888074621156",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-02T03:02:23.000Z"
    }
  ],
